# efs deployment on the fcstor test cluster

**Never use Slurm for efs.** Build/test runs on the dedicated fcstor test
environment, reached via the `efs-test-ssh` wrapper:
`~/.cursor/skills/efs-test-ssh/scripts/efs-ssh.sh <host> '<cmd>'`

**Disposable cluster (standing permission from the user, Aug 21 2026):** you
may always tear down the whole cluster and wipe all data on fcstor003–006
for testing — no rolling restart, no build-id dance, just fresh mkfs —
UNLESS the user says differently for a particular run.

**Wipe with `edelete`, NEVER `rm -rf`** (rm -rf on millions of chunk files
takes many minutes; edelete does all 6 paths on 4 nodes in seconds):
`for d in 01..06; do ~/git/ereport/edelete --delete --force /data1/$d/efs; done`
then `mkdir -p` the dirs again (edelete removes the start dir too).
Same for any big test-tree cleanup on these nodes.

## Topology (current)

- 4 servers (`efsd`), port 19810, 6 NVMe paths each
  (`/data1/01/efs` … `/data1/06/efs`), `--quota 36T --direct-io`:
  - node 1 = fcstor003 = 172.16.223.57  (primary/seed — no `--join`)
  - node 2 = fcstor004 = 172.16.223.58  (`--join 172.16.223.57:19810`)
  - node 3 = fcstor005 = 172.16.223.59  (`--join 172.16.223.57:19810`)
  - node 4 = fcstor006 = 172.16.223.60  (`--join 172.16.223.57:19810`)
- 13 clients (`efs-fuse`): fcstor003–015. fcstor003–006 run BOTH efsd + efs-fuse.
- Export `efs-test` (id=1), mounted at `/tmp/efs/mnt`.

## Deploy procedure

1. **rsync** repo to node-local scratch on each target (exclude the live mount
   + logs so `--delete` doesn't fight FUSE), run ON the node:
   `rsync -a --delete --exclude='/mnt/' --exclude='*.log' "$HOME/git/efs/" /tmp/efs/`
2. **Build on the node** (never the NFS home, never a login node):
   `cd /tmp/efs && make efsd` (servers) / `make efs-fuse` (clients).
3. **Rolling restart** — one node at a time; verify it rejoins
   (`./efs-mgmt status 172.16.223.57:19810`) before the next.

### Restart one efsd (server)
`pkill -x efsd` — exact name; NEVER `pkill -f "efsd --node-id N"` (the pattern
matches the ssh remote command and kills your own shell). Then:
`cd /tmp/efs && setsid ./efsd --node-id N --addr 172.16.223.5X --port 19810 --storage /data1/01/efs,/data1/02/efs,/data1/03/efs,/data1/04/efs,/data1/05/efs,/data1/06/efs --quota 36T --direct-io [--join 172.16.223.57:19810] >efsd.log 2>&1 </dev/null &`
Use `setsid … </dev/null &` to detach; a bare `nohup … &` can hang the ssh session.

### Restart one efs-fuse (client)
`fusermount3 -u /tmp/efs/mnt; pkill -x efs-fuse`, then:
`cd /tmp/efs && setsid ./efs-fuse 172.16.223.57:19810 efs-test /tmp/efs/mnt >fuse.log 2>&1 </dev/null &`

## Build-ID gate

`efsd` HELLO requires a matching `EFS_BUILD_ID`. Rolling restart works only
when the ID is unchanged (same commit, `-dirty`). After a NEW commit, restart
ALL servers together — mixed build IDs are rejected.
